<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcomer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 388–c. 396</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcomer was a Frankish king of the late 4th century who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunno">Sunno</a>, raided Roman territory across the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in 388. The Frankish general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arbogast">Arbogast</a>, serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, campaigned against them across the river in 392. Later the western general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stilicho">Stilicho</a> captured Marcomer and sent him into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruria">Etruria</a>.</p></div>
